.TH GIT-TWIG 1 "" "git-twig" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-twig \- lightweight Git worktrees using native copy-on-write
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git twig
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B git twig skill
.br
.B git twig -h
.br
.B git twig --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Twig creates ordinary linked Git worktrees. Supported creation requests use native
copy-on-write on macOS/APFS, Linux reflink filesystems or Windows ReFS and Dev
Drive volumes. Other requests use
Git's worktree implementation, without inheriting local or ignored files.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new [-b branch | --detach] path [commit]
Create a worktree. With a previously adopted root, new -b branch alone selects
root/branch (branch slashes become hyphens). Explicit paths keep Git semantics. Since v0.5.0, Twig can select a nearby donor worktree for
other commits; matching files are verified clones and Git writes the rest.
Unsupported options delegate to Git.
.TP
.B adopt [--dry-run] [--yes] [--compact [--offline] | --move-only] [--worktrees-dir=root] [worktree]
Discover registered worktrees and show a sibling layout under root. The original
clone occupies main regardless of its branch. Prompt for an unsaved root and
confirm every move; --dry-run changes nothing. Noninteractive use requires --yes
and an explicit or saved root. An optional target selects only that worktree.
Preserves branches, index bytes and dirty, untracked and ignored files. Refuses
cross-device moves, occupied destinations, locked registrations and submodule
relocation. Git repairs links after moves. A recovery journal is kept only when
a failure needs manual recovery.
Coordinate editors and agents before moving: stored absolute paths are not updated.
Linux then attempts safe in-place deduplication; --move-only disables sharing.
macOS interactive adoption offers optional offline compaction. Save work and close
agents, editors, builds and servers using donor/target worktrees first. Automation
requires --compact --offline --yes; --yes alone never authorizes APFS replacement.
CoW candidates are verified against current bytes and supported target metadata,
then atomically exchanged; old copies are retired only after verification. Index
entries are preserved, but inode/ctime changes may trigger a later stat refresh.
Open originals prevent retirement. Failure retains copies and a recovery journal;
do not restart agents or delete recovery files blindly. This is not live deduplication.
Explicit --prepare or --dedupe linked-worktree retain the v0.5 sharing-only modes.
The --prepare clones are never installed. No exclusive physical savings are measured.
.TP
.B list [--porcelain [-z]]
List worktrees. Porcelain is Git's stable machine-readable format.
.TP
.B remove path
Remove a worktree and its registration. Check for changes before removing it.
.TP
.B move path new-path
Move a worktree and update its registration.
.TP
.B lock [--reason text] path
Protect registration from pruning, moving or removal. Does not lock file contents.
.TP
.B unlock path
Remove registration protection.
.TP
.B prune [--dry-run] [--expire time]
Remove stale registrations, not working directories. Preview with --dry-run.
.TP
.B repair [path ...]
Repair repository/worktree links after manual moves, not contents or conflicts.
.TP
.B skill
Print the bundled agent instructions, including the command reference.
.SH EXAMPLE
From the directory containing the source checkout named main:
.PP
.nf
git -C main twig new -b feat/x ../feat-x HEAD
.fi
.PP
The destination is resolved relative to main, so it is a sibling named feat-x.
The requested commit is pinned; donor files never authorize uncommitted content.
.SH CHECKOUT COVERAGE
Version 0.4.0 supports common LF policies such as text=auto eol=lf.
Private candidate bytes are compared to raw target blobs. Git materializes
files requiring conversion or whose bytes differ; other verified files retain
sharing. Upgrade older releases for the released LF-policy and filter-state fixes.
Since v0.5.0, Twig materializes builtin ident and encoding exceptions per file.
Git creates empty gitlink directories without copying or initializing donor
submodules. Conversion rules do not rewrite symlink text or gitlink directories.
External filters on regular files, conditional config includes, sparse checkout
and relative attribute-file configuration delegate to stock Git.
Checkout configuration and external attributes must not change during creation.
.SH STAGING
Staging is stored under the common Git directory in twigs/staging. Successful
operations remove their own staging, as do SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP before
registration. Other failed or interrupted attempts retain diagnostic state;
inspect reported paths and registrations before retrying or deleting.
The selected donor, destination and Git metadata must share a clone-capable filesystem for
the native path; unsupported layouts delegate to Git.
.SH HELP
Short help works outside repositories:
.PP
.nf
git twig -h
git twig new --help
.fi
.PP
Git turns top-level git twig --help into this manual lookup. Homebrew installs
the manual; Cargo, Scoop and Windows installations can use git twig -h or
git-twig --help instead.
See git-worktree(1) for the complete delegated Git option reference.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TWIG_TRACE=1
Report native backend selection, verified file clone and Git-written counts,
staging and fallback reasons to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-worktree (1),
.BR git (1)
